sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    title Email + Password Login with TOTP MFA — Happy Path

    participant C as Client (Browser)
    participant NX as Next.js
    participant API as Auth API (NestJS)
    participant R as Redis (ElastiCache)
    participant M as MongoDB Atlas
    participant SES as AWS SES

    C->>NX: POST /api/auth/login { email, password }
    NX->>API: Forward request (internal VPC)

    note over API,R: Rate limit checks (shared counters across all API instances)
    API->>R: GET login_fail_account:{email}
    R-->>API: count (e.g. 1 of 5 allowed)
    API->>R: GET login_fail_ip:{ip}
    R-->>API: count (e.g. 3 of 100 allowed)

    API->>M: users.findOne({ email: "user@example.com" })
    M-->>API: user document

    note over API: bcrypt.compare(password, user.passwordHash) ~300ms async
    API->>API: Verify password (bcrypt cost 12)

    note over API,R: MFA Challenge — prove password before issuing full session
    API->>R: SET mfa_challenge:{challengeId} {userId, exp:+5min}
    API-->>C: 200 { status: "MFA_REQUIRED", mfaChallenge: "ch_abc" }

    C->>API: POST /api/auth/mfa/verify { challengeId, totpToken }
    API->>R: GET mfa_challenge:{challengeId}
    R-->>API: { userId }
    API->>API: TOTP.verify(token, secret, ±30s tolerance)

    note over API: Device fingerprint for suspicious login detection
    API->>API: Compute Device_Fingerprint (UA + Accept-Language + platform)
    API->>API: Compare vs user.deviceFingerprints (90-day window)

    alt Suspicious login (new device or country)
        API--)SES: Async: Send security alert email (non-blocking)
    end

    note over API,R: Issue tokens and create session
    API->>API: generateRefreshToken() → 256-bit opaque random
    API->>API: generateAccessToken(user, kid:v2) → JWT HS256 (15min)
    API->>R: HSET session:{sessionId} { userId, SHA256(refreshToken), familyId, familyVersion:1, fingerprint, ip, ua }
    API->>R: SADD user_sessions:{userId} sessionId
    API->>R: DEL login_fail_account:{email}

    note over API,M: Append-only audit entry
    API->>M: audit_logs.insertOne({ event:'login_success', userId, ip, ua, correlationId })

    API-->>NX: 200 { accessToken } + Set-Cookie: refreshToken; HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Strict; Path=/api/auth/refresh
    NX-->>C: Auth response + cookie
    note over C: accessToken stored in Zustand (memory only — never localStorage)
